{
	"@id": "git-discipline",
	"@context": "tb",
	"data": "Concept: Git Discipline\n\nThe Rule\nCommit and push to Forgejo after any file change in the workspace or projects. No exceptions.\n\nWhy\nFiles are memory. An uncommitted change is a mental note — it doesn't survive restarts, crashes, or context loss. The push is the write.\n\nHow\nUse conventional commits: feat:, fix:, docs:, refactor:, chore:\nEvery project in ~/projects/ gets a Forgejo repo from the start\nCreate the repo on Forgejo first, then push — no orphaned local repos\nNever commit: .venv/,…",
